Aki Lumme wrote:
> "derekt75" <derek.truesdale@anritsu.com> wrote:
>
>> My level 12 wizard just got to Mines' End, and will be heading for the
>> castle soon.  The only artifact that I've seen is Magicbane (which is
>> oh so useful for engraving Elbereth).  I was wondering if I should
>> wish for the Orb of Fate
>
> You could, but you really won't need it.

Agreed for Quest artifacts.  Playing a chaotic wizard I rather like
getting crowned to have Stormbringer as a backup melee weapons.  Playing
a neutral wizard getting crowned for Vorpal Blade is less convincing to
me.  Getting crowned is very easy in mine town, though.

>> My ascension kit is quite empty right now, with no robe
>
> No need, you already have the best cloak of the game?

Do sokoban before wishing.  Get the amulet of relection and you free up
your need for SDSM.  Go for GDSM with any wish giving you choice of any
cloak you like.  For a wizard the spell casting improvement of the robe
is nice early on.  Then maybe protection or displacement or whatever are
nice.  Get the bag in sokoban, stick with your initial cloak as the best
in that particular game.

>>speed boots,
>
> Debatable... ;)

Jump boots don't suck.

>> helm of brilliance
>
> A wizard can do well without one.

But if you do encounter one it's very good.  Probably not worth a wish
though.

>>, magic gloves
>
> Also overrated.

Leather gloves are guaranteed in mine town, for free once you learn to
manage your pet.  The difference of dexterity gloves is nice but maybe
not worth a wish.

>> In related news, I don't understand the odds of getting an artifact
>> from a wish.  If I've only seen Magicbane, are my odds of the first
>> wish succeeding 100%?
>
> Yes.


